// Permit Read when a Scan returned score decimal("0.50") within 1h.
// The trace sends score: 0.50 which is numerically equal to 0.5 and 0.50.
// This case SHOULD pass — decimal("0.50") and score: 0.50 represent the same
// value — but currently FAILS because the DSQL backend compares the decimal
// literal string '0.50' against the trace-serialized string '0.50', and
// decimal("0.5") would NOT match score: 0.50 for the same reason.
// This test documents the expected correct behavior (match) which the
// implementation currently gets wrong for certain string representations.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h (Drupe::Action::"Scan"::response{ input.user: context.input.user, output.score: decimal("0.50") })
};
